### ===== VARIABILI =====
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@graphqlUrl = http://localhost:8080/graphql

### ===== AUTH =====

### Registrazione nuovo utente
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "firstName": "Mario",
  "lastName": "Rossi"
}

### Login (salva il token nella risposta)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Salva il token dalla risposta del login
@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### ===== TEST SICUREZZA =====

### Test 1: Accesso SENZA token (deve dare 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me

### Test 2: Accesso CON token (deve funzionare)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{aauthToken}}

### Test 3: Accesso endpoint ADMIN senza ruolo ADMIN (deve dare 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ===== ENDPOINT PUBBLICI (senza token) =====

### Lista categorie (pubblico)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories

### Eventi pubblicati (pubblico)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/public?page=0&size=10

### Venue per città (pubblico)
GET {{baseUrl}}/venues/city/Milano?page=0&size=10

### ===== GRAPHQL =====

### Query GraphQL senza auth (categorie - pubblico)
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "{ categories { id name description } }"
}

### Query GraphQL con auth (my orders)
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "query": "{ myOrders(page: 0, size: 10) { content { id orderNumber status totalAmount } pageInfo { totalElements } } }"
}

### Query me (richiede auth)
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "query": "{ me { id email firstName lastName role } }"
}